WEBVTT

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:35.994 --> 00:37.620
I heard it's your first time.

00:37.704 --> 00:40.498
5 YEARS AGO

00:40.582 --> 00:42.709
How desperate must you be
to do something like this?

00:43.585 --> 00:44.753
I'm just curious.

00:46.546 --> 00:48.506
Isn't marriage supposed to be romantic?

00:49.883 --> 00:51.426
Romance might be a stretch,

00:52.469 --> 00:54.220
but there is a natural order to things.

00:54.888 --> 00:57.640
You go through the motions,
then mate with someone at your level.

00:58.308 --> 01:02.187
By following the natural order,
a marriage earns society's approval.

01:02.270 --> 01:03.229
Wouldn't you agree?

01:04.522 --> 01:05.774
I guess I figured,

01:06.399 --> 01:07.734
"Fuck the natural order."

01:09.527 --> 01:12.614
What's so special about putting two names
on a piece of paper?

01:12.697 --> 01:16.409
It's actually a proclamation
of mutual distrust…

01:18.745 --> 01:21.122
with both parties knowing
it won't last forever.

01:22.248 --> 01:24.667
It's no more than a means
to tie each other down.

01:26.711 --> 01:27.712
Romance?

01:29.923 --> 01:31.591
What's romantic about a contract?

01:33.593 --> 01:35.553
What's so romantic about a certificate?

01:37.430 --> 01:39.099
None of that crap means anything.

01:44.896 --> 01:47.107
You must have a lot of issues
with marriage.

01:47.190 --> 01:48.024
No.

01:48.775 --> 01:50.110
The idea of marriage just…

01:52.695 --> 01:53.571
disgusts me.

01:56.783 --> 01:58.284
This was a bad idea.

02:00.036 --> 02:01.037
Let's call this off.

02:02.413 --> 02:05.458
I'll be dead in six months.
Four at the soonest.

02:12.340 --> 02:14.425
You would be my first and last wife.

02:15.468 --> 02:16.970
If you're okay with that…

02:19.430 --> 02:20.473
will you marry me?

02:28.648 --> 02:34.571
THE TRUNK

02:36.781 --> 02:38.116
Don't you recognize me?

02:39.284 --> 02:40.118
Of course I do.

02:41.828 --> 02:43.121
How do you know me?

02:45.248 --> 02:46.207
It's not important.

02:55.758 --> 02:59.679
A senior I knew had plans to study abroad
but committed suicide because of you.

03:00.763 --> 03:03.099
They said dying
was the only way to escape from you.

03:04.350 --> 03:06.144
It sounds like I was a real bitch.

03:08.104 --> 03:10.940
That's just how I know of you,
not necessarily how I think of you.

03:12.775 --> 03:13.610
Meaning?

03:15.403 --> 03:17.989
Who knows what goes on
in the mind of someone

03:18.948 --> 03:21.075
who's decided to disappear from the world?

03:23.328 --> 03:25.121
Maybe they just needed an excuse.

03:29.167 --> 03:32.587
But that doesn't mean
I'm convinced you're not a bitch.

03:35.548 --> 03:36.591
I also remember you…

03:38.551 --> 03:39.594
from back then, Ms. In-ji.

03:42.430 --> 03:44.057
But the reason doesn't really matter,

03:45.808 --> 03:47.936
so I'll tell you later
when I get a chance.

04:09.540 --> 04:11.251
Don't get out. I was just leaving.

04:11.834 --> 04:12.919
Were you visiting our house?

04:14.587 --> 04:15.421
"Our house"?

04:17.423 --> 04:19.634
It's weird hearing you call it that.

04:21.636 --> 04:23.054
I met your wife.

04:24.222 --> 04:25.056
Did you?

04:25.807 --> 04:26.641
What did you think?

04:27.141 --> 04:27.976
She just

04:29.227 --> 04:30.895
looks like someone's wife.

04:32.438 --> 04:34.274
So you didn't know each other
before today?

04:35.733 --> 04:36.567
Actually,

04:38.069 --> 04:40.405
it turns out we went to college together.

04:43.658 --> 04:45.994
I wish I could trust you too.

04:46.828 --> 04:48.496
So hang in there, even when it's hard.

05:12.353 --> 05:13.938
She came because of the lights.

05:14.480 --> 05:18.651
Ms. Lee Seo-yeon had some tea
and stayed for 20 minutes or so.

05:19.861 --> 05:21.029
I didn't ask.

05:21.112 --> 05:23.281
I would want to ask if I were you.

05:26.242 --> 05:27.618
I can take you to the hospital.

05:27.702 --> 05:30.330
My appointment's next week.
I'm going out on personal business now.

06:03.196 --> 06:05.073
Do you still dabble in you know what?

06:06.366 --> 06:07.742
I need an expert.

06:27.553 --> 06:28.596
Does he beat you?

06:29.389 --> 06:30.807
Let's cut to the chase.

06:31.391 --> 06:32.433
Rude-ass southerner.

06:32.934 --> 06:34.685
At least ask me how I'm doing.

06:36.521 --> 06:37.772
I was curious how you were.

06:39.649 --> 06:42.026
How is your new post,
Assistant Manager Yoo In-yeong?

06:47.907 --> 06:48.950
I'm pregnant.

06:50.576 --> 06:53.996
I like the idea of having a family.
Maybe because mine's all dead.

06:55.331 --> 06:56.499
Do you have family?

06:56.582 --> 06:58.960
Does your husband know?

07:00.461 --> 07:01.421
I sure hope not.

07:02.672 --> 07:05.258
You might be better off
without a so-called family.

07:06.467 --> 07:07.593
Then why look for him?

07:08.094 --> 07:11.389
Wasn't it enough to find out
he's well and didn't die a year ago?

07:11.889 --> 07:13.933
Works for me, as long as I'm getting paid.

07:14.475 --> 07:16.227
Do you plan on marrying him again?

07:18.187 --> 07:20.648
Or are you going to kill him?
That I could get behind.

07:23.776 --> 07:24.944
Where is he?

07:29.782 --> 07:31.075
According to the broker,

07:31.159 --> 07:33.911
he was in Prague,
and then moved to Hungary two weeks ago.

07:34.454 --> 07:35.580
Budapest, to be exact.

07:39.000 --> 07:40.626
Please keep me posted as usual.

07:44.589 --> 07:47.133
I sometimes dream
about finding my younger sibling's corpse.

07:48.843 --> 07:52.305
Some days, I can kind of make them out,

07:53.639 --> 07:54.849
other days,

07:54.932 --> 07:57.143
they're just a bloody mess
of skin and bone.

07:58.269 --> 08:00.021
But the dreams give me peace of mind.

08:01.189 --> 08:03.232
It's the what-ifs that drive us insane.

08:06.861 --> 08:08.488
What sort of dreams do you have?

08:12.617 --> 08:13.910
I don't have dreams.

08:26.797 --> 08:29.717
BUDAPEST

09:22.853 --> 09:25.147
I guess you've forgotten…

09:28.192 --> 09:29.485
what day it is today.

10:20.953 --> 10:22.163
Fuck me.

10:42.933 --> 10:44.518
HAN JEONG-WON

10:46.937 --> 10:48.981
Yeah, it turns out that I had it.

10:49.482 --> 10:51.192
I found it while I was cleaning.

10:51.275 --> 10:53.069
It's your prized possession, after all.

10:58.240 --> 10:59.575
Sure, I'll bring it then.

12:32.793 --> 12:33.878
It doesn't hurt,

12:35.421 --> 12:37.006
if that's what's bothering you.

13:10.664 --> 13:11.999
Excuse me, coming through.

13:17.296 --> 13:18.130
Going down.

13:21.175 --> 13:23.636
Ignore everything else
and just look at the numbers.

13:27.640 --> 13:28.974
They're just numbers.

14:04.760 --> 14:07.638
Should we schedule Ms. Noh
to see a plastic surgeon next month?

14:08.556 --> 14:09.390
Yes, sure.

14:09.473 --> 14:12.768
- When might be a good date?
- Just a moment, sorry.

14:15.604 --> 14:17.106
WIFE

14:18.357 --> 14:20.985
Sorry, I'll call you back later.
I'm at the hospital.

14:21.485 --> 14:23.696
Do you need any paperwork
for insurance purposes?

14:23.779 --> 14:26.740
- No, it's fine.
- Okay, then I'll assist you with payment.

14:28.909 --> 14:29.743
Thank you.

14:41.714 --> 14:43.966
Wait here. I'll go get your meds.

14:57.438 --> 15:00.065
I've seen countless people
get hurt and torn apart,

15:00.608 --> 15:02.026
but never seen someone heal.

15:05.404 --> 15:06.572
I don't want to see it…

15:08.616 --> 15:12.578
but I think the stitches
will be etched in my mind if I don't.

15:18.792 --> 15:22.171
I know you're no crybaby,
but can you at least try to whine a bit?

15:23.339 --> 15:26.133
That might just put my mind at ease.

15:38.646 --> 15:39.813
Are you free in two days?

15:42.900 --> 15:45.903
If you don't have any plans,
we should get married then.

15:58.248 --> 16:00.501
NO RECENT MISSED CALLS

16:03.212 --> 16:05.631
Sorry, I'll call you back later.
I'm at the hospital.

16:15.891 --> 16:18.769
What is this mess?
Did you kids really eat all this?

16:20.729 --> 16:22.982
Guys, didn't mommy tell you
no snacks at night?

16:23.065 --> 16:25.109
Come out and brush your teeth.

16:25.192 --> 16:26.485
- No messing around!
- Sucker!

16:26.568 --> 16:28.195
- Don't mess around!
- Come here!

16:32.825 --> 16:35.744
My mom texted yesterday.
What should we do about the rice cakes?

16:38.080 --> 16:40.958
Why on earth did I ever get married?

16:42.543 --> 16:44.128
Because I was the best of the worst

16:45.546 --> 16:47.715
out of all the class-eight guys at W&L.

16:47.798 --> 16:51.468
I swear I'm as stable as they come,
but somehow my life's still a mess.

16:52.511 --> 16:55.556
You want me to buy you something?
Keep it under two million.

16:59.727 --> 17:01.437
What's the name of Mr. Han's new wife?

17:02.021 --> 17:04.064
- Why do you ask?
- I want to get to know her.

17:04.148 --> 17:05.024
Why?

17:05.107 --> 17:10.029
I've got nothing going for me. No career,
no inheritance, no high-salary husband.

17:10.112 --> 17:13.615
You're a CEO with just a 5% stake,
so my connections are my only pride.

17:31.258 --> 17:33.969
It's just standard procedure.
Per the manual.

17:50.027 --> 17:51.111
The manual…

17:53.697 --> 17:56.450
Hey, Yoon-a said--

17:56.533 --> 17:59.036
Isn't it about time you got a new car?
I'll buy you one.

17:59.578 --> 18:01.330
Just give me
30 minutes of your time tomorrow.

18:01.413 --> 18:04.083
What is it this time?
What kind of trouble are you in?

18:04.917 --> 18:06.293
I'm getting married tomorrow.

18:07.336 --> 18:09.296
They need a witness for the ceremony.

18:09.379 --> 18:12.883
Weren't you skipping the ceremony?
And a witness for what?

18:13.550 --> 18:16.261
Tomorrow at 3:00.
They'll send you an invite.

18:16.970 --> 18:17.846
Who will?

18:31.568 --> 18:33.028
How are your wife's injuries?

18:34.655 --> 18:36.865
She's doing better now.
She had her stitches removed.

18:38.117 --> 18:39.576
Doctors say she's healing fast.

18:39.660 --> 18:43.038
I'm not sure whether that's true
or if she's just good at masking pain.

18:44.331 --> 18:46.041
You went with her to the hospital?

18:47.209 --> 18:49.920
You didn't know
that we went to the hospital together?

18:54.800 --> 18:56.009
Her injury was my fault.

18:58.595 --> 18:59.429
I'm glad.

19:00.931 --> 19:02.599
You two seem to be bonding.

19:10.524 --> 19:12.401
OH SE-EUN
OUR LOVER/THE ORPHAN/YOU

19:28.375 --> 19:30.919
It's a souvenir
to remind us of our worst moment.

19:33.297 --> 19:34.715
How does it feel seeing it again?

19:46.560 --> 19:47.728
That's just cruel.

19:48.854 --> 19:49.688
How could you…

19:50.564 --> 19:53.275
Those pills aren't for you to take.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.279
I want you to resist.

20:02.951 --> 20:04.286
I'll do as you say.

20:07.247 --> 20:08.457
I'm getting married tomorrow.

20:21.345 --> 20:22.471
INBOX
NM: INVITATION

20:22.554 --> 20:24.139
GROOM HAN JEONG-WON
BRIDE NOH IN-JI

20:26.683 --> 20:29.895
AS THE WITNESS TO THIS WEDDING,
PLEASE NOTE THE FOLLOWING RULES

20:33.565 --> 20:36.735
You call this a wedding invitation?
It's more like blackmail.

21:22.114 --> 21:24.074
How'd I put these on back then?

21:39.798 --> 21:41.425
I could have been undressed.

21:41.925 --> 21:44.886
If you weren't dressed by now,
you'd be planning to bail.

21:46.888 --> 21:48.432
The thought crossed my mind.

21:48.515 --> 21:50.642
I had no idea I'd be doing all this again.

21:51.601 --> 21:54.187
The ceremony is meant to take place
after a week of acclimation.

21:54.730 --> 21:56.481
Ours was delayed due to the accident.

21:58.317 --> 21:59.693
It's all in the manual.

22:00.319 --> 22:03.196
I thought I would be spared all the pomp,
but I guess not.

22:19.171 --> 22:21.298
You're pretty good at this.

22:21.381 --> 22:22.841
I'm good at other things too.

22:25.761 --> 22:29.639
My grandmother always said
that I was born with deft fingers,

22:30.974 --> 22:34.853
and that people with deft fingers
end up doing things they don't need to.

22:35.687 --> 22:38.440
Apparently, they are destined
to shed a lot of tears.

22:39.399 --> 22:40.567
Have you?

22:43.612 --> 22:44.446
No.

22:50.160 --> 22:52.162
I was going to wear this to the funeral.

22:52.245 --> 22:53.997
I knew these were mourning clothes.

22:54.498 --> 22:57.667
The only black suit in the wardrobe
of someone who never wears suits.

22:58.668 --> 23:01.546
I figured it'd be of comfort
to someone who wishes their father dead.

23:04.508 --> 23:07.469
Think of it like signing
a one-year insurance contract.

23:08.720 --> 23:10.764
One that can simply be terminated
for a fee.

23:13.433 --> 23:14.267
Insurance?

23:20.232 --> 23:21.358
Let's go.

23:41.086 --> 23:45.590
The space you're looking at now
is the library. So over here…

23:46.341 --> 23:48.844
It's not too late.
Say the word, and I won't do it.

23:58.895 --> 24:03.442
This wedding ceremony is to reaffirm
the contract between the two of you.

24:04.109 --> 24:10.073
This contract is confidential between NM,
Mr. Han Jeong-won, and Ms. Noh In-ji.

24:10.824 --> 24:16.496
Legally, this marriage will leave you
with no obligations or records.

24:17.747 --> 24:22.294
In case of breach of contract,
both parties may face civil liability

24:22.377 --> 24:24.921
as stated in your contract with NM.

24:26.298 --> 24:27.674
The marriage will last a year,

24:28.258 --> 24:31.136
but if the two of you agree,
it can be extended.

24:32.512 --> 24:35.932
However, if one side objects,
an extension is void,

24:36.516 --> 24:37.392
and from then on,

24:38.643 --> 24:40.604
you may never contact each other again.

24:42.147 --> 24:45.734
This marriage will begin
the moment you sign the contract.

25:09.049 --> 25:11.176
Mr. Han Jeong-won and Mrs. Noh In-ji,

25:11.259 --> 25:14.095
I now pronounce you husband and wife,
per the contract by NM.

25:14.721 --> 25:18.099
I'm honored to join you both
in your marriage.

25:28.318 --> 25:34.991
MARRIAGE AGREEMENT
GROOM HAN JEONG-WON, BRIDE NOH IN-JI

26:09.109 --> 26:10.402
What did you do before this?

26:11.361 --> 26:13.071
According to protocol, I can't tell you.

26:14.864 --> 26:15.699
Protocol?

26:17.659 --> 26:19.369
Your legal team did seem sharp.

26:19.452 --> 26:22.205
They'd win a case
arguing that Messi plays for Spain.

26:25.667 --> 26:27.460
Why do other people do this?

26:27.544 --> 26:31.715
Did you ever ask your former husbands
why they did this?

26:35.176 --> 26:36.553
I've given it some thought,

26:38.138 --> 26:40.724
and I can see how a lonely,
terminally ill patient

26:41.474 --> 26:42.767
might give this a go.

26:43.268 --> 26:45.979
Still, what's the point
of a fake marriage?

26:47.480 --> 26:49.941
Maybe they wish to hide their loneliness
so desperately,

26:50.025 --> 26:52.068
they're willing to cling to a facade.

26:54.487 --> 26:56.948
Having company doesn't hide loneliness.

26:57.824 --> 26:59.826
They know, but they grow accustomed to it.

27:00.368 --> 27:02.871
It's like a habit,
like they're afraid to be alone.

27:03.830 --> 27:05.957
Wasn't that why you got married?

27:09.169 --> 27:11.463
Like a habit or separation anxiety,

27:12.589 --> 27:15.091
fully aware of the fact
that you'd feel alone anyway.

27:21.598 --> 27:22.432
Good night.

27:24.100 --> 27:25.018
Whatever the case,

27:26.144 --> 27:28.313
it is our first official night
as newlyweds.

27:40.283 --> 27:43.119
IT'S NOT TOO LATE
SAY THE WORD, AND I WON'T DO IT

30:04.385 --> 30:05.720
Were you drowning?

30:08.306 --> 30:09.891
Seemed like that kind of dream.

30:12.769 --> 30:14.020
It's the same old dream.

30:16.189 --> 30:17.398
Don't worry.

30:19.692 --> 30:21.653
The tidal waves can't reach you here.

31:27.719 --> 31:29.178
Last night, did you…

31:37.103 --> 31:37.937
Never mind.

31:38.688 --> 31:40.064
I think I had sleep paralysis.

31:41.399 --> 31:44.360
If you want to know
if I was by your side last night, I was.

31:48.364 --> 31:50.992
The manual says
to share a room after the wedding.

31:53.745 --> 31:54.996
Were you drowning?

31:56.497 --> 31:58.082
Seemed like that kind of dream.

31:59.459 --> 32:00.710
It's the same old dream.

32:05.840 --> 32:06.841
Don't worry.

32:09.010 --> 32:10.929
The tidal waves can't reach you here.

32:20.521 --> 32:23.483
Except in special circumstances,
the couple sleeps together.

32:24.776 --> 32:25.902
Special circumstances?

32:26.402 --> 32:28.988
Like diseases
classified as "highly infectious."

32:39.916 --> 32:41.417
Why is she taking it this far?

32:42.377 --> 32:44.379
I may need a woman, but not like this.

32:55.390 --> 32:57.183
I'm already a train wreck.

32:58.559 --> 33:02.230
Ask Lee Seo-yeon how broken
I need to be for her to feel satisfied.

33:03.147 --> 33:06.317
All I asked of you
was to let a year pass by quietly.

33:06.401 --> 33:08.069
Was that too much to ask?

33:08.695 --> 33:10.321
What's making you so nervous?

33:10.405 --> 33:12.615
Nervous? I just don't want to care
about any of this!

33:13.116 --> 33:15.618
I want things to go back to how they were,
as soon as possible!

33:17.286 --> 33:19.163
Do you really want to go back?

33:20.331 --> 33:21.165
Yes!

33:22.834 --> 33:23.668
I understand.

33:27.171 --> 33:31.009
I'll see what we can do
about our sleeping arrangement.

34:14.677 --> 34:16.512
- How did they do that?
- He lifted her.

34:18.890 --> 34:20.516
- I got you.
- Yeah, you have.

34:20.600 --> 34:22.727
- Turn and do that thing.
- How?

34:22.810 --> 34:25.354
- Try to do something with your leg.
- Wait, like this?

34:29.150 --> 34:30.735
Now, turn! Go on!

34:31.277 --> 34:34.864
- Spin around like this?
- And then spin me like this.

34:34.947 --> 34:36.532
- That's it, go low.
- Lower me.

34:36.616 --> 34:38.201
- Lower me down.
- Like this?

34:39.577 --> 34:42.246
- Come on, don't let go!
- Hold up.

34:47.376 --> 34:50.129
The lights shipped from Paris.
I'll replace them next week.

34:51.589 --> 34:53.841
Congratulations on your marriage, honey.

35:15.988 --> 35:17.657
I'd like to inquire about some drugs.

35:18.741 --> 35:20.827
The contents may be different
from what's on the label.

35:21.702 --> 35:23.037
I'll send them via express mail.

35:47.520 --> 35:49.272
What brings you here so early?

35:49.856 --> 35:51.732
Hasn't it been a while since you cooked?

35:52.692 --> 35:54.777
Is that bastard returning from the grave?

35:56.529 --> 35:57.697
Glare at me all you want.

35:58.197 --> 35:59.157
Give me some too.

36:00.449 --> 36:02.743
I know it's going down my own gullet,

36:04.537 --> 36:05.913
but eating is such a chore.

36:07.415 --> 36:09.667
Your kimchi went too sour and wilted,
so I threw it out.

36:10.168 --> 36:12.670
I just winged this batch,
but it tastes damn good.

36:14.463 --> 36:16.090
I don't cook for it to be eaten.

36:16.841 --> 36:18.801
So you make it just to throw it away?

36:18.885 --> 36:20.636
I don't like the house feeling empty.

36:21.429 --> 36:22.263
Hold up.

36:22.889 --> 36:24.599
I heard that jerk told the realtor

36:25.099 --> 36:26.976
to leave this place alone
until you move out.

36:27.935 --> 36:30.730
Jesus, you guys are something else.

36:32.773 --> 36:33.900
Have some stew.

36:33.983 --> 36:35.610
Why don't you eat before you go?

36:35.693 --> 36:37.069
I'll eat at the office.

36:39.155 --> 36:41.240
But this baby radish kimchi is delicious.

36:57.548 --> 37:00.468
"She came by just nowww"? Darn typo…

37:00.551 --> 37:02.553
And I've got red pepper powder everywhere.

37:04.680 --> 37:07.308
We'll be blooming these flowers now,
so follow along slowly.

37:10.019 --> 37:12.146
Just go with the flow, like this.

37:13.022 --> 37:16.067
Now, we're going to move
the finished flower over

37:17.526 --> 37:20.780
by supporting the base of the flower
with these garden shears

37:21.405 --> 37:23.699
and removing the nail slowly.

37:23.783 --> 37:25.743
Then you simply place it…

37:29.163 --> 37:30.164
wherever you'd like.

37:32.166 --> 37:33.167
Would you like to try?

37:34.293 --> 37:36.045
His work is so delicate,
like a true master.

37:39.257 --> 37:41.342
- Absolutely stunning.
- Goodness!

37:42.510 --> 37:45.638
His makeshift methods may stir curiosity,
but they're far from traditional.

37:47.056 --> 37:49.016
Tradition takes time to develop, you know.

37:49.517 --> 37:51.852
When will the lights arrive from France?

37:52.770 --> 37:54.230
Can I come over to see them?

37:56.357 --> 37:58.693
They're the only set in the country,
after all.

37:59.193 --> 38:00.861
I'll never get another chance.

38:03.114 --> 38:05.574
I'm not sure. It's not up to me, really.

38:07.410 --> 38:09.078
I'll take that as a yes from you.

38:16.544 --> 38:19.797
Thank you for the great class.
I can't wait for the next one.

38:20.298 --> 38:21.299
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

38:22.883 --> 38:26.470
I ordered some birthday rice cakes
under the name Oh Hyeon-cheol.

38:26.554 --> 38:27.513
Right.

38:28.014 --> 38:31.892
Please prepare them carefully.
They're for a picky bunch.

38:32.560 --> 38:34.562
If anything goes wrong,
I'll be the one to blame.

38:35.771 --> 38:36.731
Is he your husband?

38:37.857 --> 38:38.858
Sorry?

38:38.941 --> 38:40.359
I assume it's not your name.

38:41.235 --> 38:43.571
Right, they're for
my father-in-law's birthday.

38:44.155 --> 38:46.407
I get it. You don't like
dealing with your in-laws.

38:48.451 --> 38:49.577
Don't worry.

38:49.660 --> 38:51.412
I'll make your in-laws say,

38:51.495 --> 38:53.539
"I'm not sure about everything else, but

38:55.333 --> 38:56.667
the rice cakes were good."

39:02.298 --> 39:03.215
Wow.

39:19.106 --> 39:21.817
I had to get roped into
this 50-million-won trunk fiasco.

39:22.318 --> 39:25.696
My gut tells me that all our hard work
on this case will get us nowhere.

39:28.199 --> 39:29.075
The fingerprints?

39:30.117 --> 39:31.869
They were underwater, so it'll take time.

39:37.416 --> 39:38.334
What is it now?

39:40.461 --> 39:42.088
There's a lot going on here,

39:43.005 --> 39:44.256
but there's also nothing.

39:44.965 --> 39:47.051
It's too clean, as if someone's tidied up.

39:48.969 --> 39:49.970
What are you saying?

39:52.348 --> 39:53.516
I don't know, okay?

39:59.647 --> 40:00.606
Hello?

40:02.274 --> 40:03.692
They found out who owns the trunk.

40:09.949 --> 40:12.493
You must have a lot of items like this
lying around.

40:12.576 --> 40:15.204
This costs over 50 million,
yet you had no idea it was missing.

40:18.582 --> 40:20.418
You didn't use it yourself, did you?

40:22.962 --> 40:25.631
It was found with the deceased.

40:31.929 --> 40:35.057
How do you know the owner of the trunk?

40:38.144 --> 40:39.186
I'm her husband.

40:41.480 --> 40:42.773
My wife used to use it.

40:46.485 --> 40:47.445
Which wife?

40:56.954 --> 40:59.832
I'll keep watch, so you're free to go.
It's going to get dusty.

41:19.685 --> 41:21.896
He seems to be looking for
a house in Budapest.

41:25.983 --> 41:27.902
I think he plans on settling down.

41:38.329 --> 41:40.164
I'd like to take the old lights.

41:41.123 --> 41:42.208
- Is that okay?
- Sure.

41:43.626 --> 41:47.505
It's an antique piece with artistic value.
Don't you think Jeong-won…

41:49.256 --> 41:51.800
I mean, shouldn't you discuss it
with your husband?

41:51.884 --> 41:54.678
You know very well he loathes that thing.

41:55.513 --> 41:58.349
I had been wondering
how to get rid of it anyway.

42:00.351 --> 42:02.353
Why don't we have dinner as a group
with our spouses?

42:03.687 --> 42:07.107
What with changing the lights
and your wedding,

42:07.191 --> 42:08.359
a celebration is due.

42:09.193 --> 42:10.986
Or not, if you're uncomfortable.

42:12.029 --> 42:13.656
Of course not. Let's do it.

42:14.156 --> 42:15.908
How does next Wednesday sound?

42:16.867 --> 42:18.661
Sure, sounds good to me.

42:21.413 --> 42:22.248
Oh my!

42:23.666 --> 42:25.209
Here you both are.

42:28.712 --> 42:30.923
I've heard a lot about you
from my husband.

42:31.006 --> 42:32.967
I'm Kang Yoon-a.

42:33.968 --> 42:34.802
Right.

42:43.686 --> 42:48.190
She seems easygoing,
classy, and not too talkative.

42:48.691 --> 42:51.318
I was worried she might be a whack job.
Good thing she's not, right?

42:52.027 --> 42:54.530
Mr. Han doesn't look the type,
but he's got an eye for nice women.

42:57.491 --> 42:58.701
Are you doing okay?

42:59.326 --> 43:00.160
Of course.

43:00.786 --> 43:02.621
It's about time Jeong-won was happy.

43:13.424 --> 43:16.176
We'll be having Lee Seo-yeon
and her husband over for dinner.

43:21.265 --> 43:22.182
Are you two close?

43:22.766 --> 43:24.727
She did help us replace the lights,

43:25.644 --> 43:26.604
so I agreed to it.

44:12.024 --> 44:14.860
I was going to sell it to a junkyard
for 3,000 won,

44:16.153 --> 44:18.238
but she offered to take it, so I let her.

44:18.864 --> 44:21.200
Why 3,000 won?
It's worth well over 30 million.

44:22.117 --> 44:24.703
I didn't want it to be remembered
as something of value.

44:25.204 --> 44:27.414
I wanted it to become junk
worth only 3,000 won,

44:27.915 --> 44:31.543
then be torn apart and melted bit by bit
until eventually nothing remained.

44:33.379 --> 44:35.714
Now, annoyingly,
it will live on for years to come.

44:42.971 --> 44:45.516
Seriously, what did you do
before this job?

44:47.559 --> 44:48.602
A lot of things.

44:50.437 --> 44:51.730
Just tell me one.

44:53.732 --> 44:55.609
I once taught dancing.

44:55.693 --> 44:58.737
Tango, waltz, and all that jazz.

44:59.863 --> 45:01.281
Let me guess, milonga?

45:04.702 --> 45:06.787
There was a USB drive
plugged into the car.

45:09.873 --> 45:11.208
Why do you go out at dawn?

45:14.336 --> 45:15.295
To exercise.

45:16.505 --> 45:17.631
What kind of exercise?

45:21.677 --> 45:22.761
Kayaking.

45:24.304 --> 45:26.056
No one else is ever out that early,

45:27.057 --> 45:29.143
so I feel like an island
floating alone on the lake.

45:31.687 --> 45:32.938
You sure get up to a lot.

45:36.400 --> 45:38.694
This was the best I could do
about our sleeping arrangement.

45:39.528 --> 45:41.447
Think of us as peaceful islands.

45:42.906 --> 45:45.284
In exchange,
I'll block any tidal waves for you.

46:45.385 --> 46:46.720
What are you doing here alone?

46:48.847 --> 46:50.390
Seeing where the newlyweds sleep.

46:51.558 --> 46:53.268
What about it did you want to see?

46:55.729 --> 46:58.315
Maybe it's the diffuser,
but it smells different.

46:58.941 --> 47:00.025
Is it bergamot?

47:00.526 --> 47:01.693
I like the new lights.

47:02.694 --> 47:03.779
Thank you.

47:04.696 --> 47:06.198
Did you even get a proper look at them?

47:36.395 --> 47:38.564
- Doesn't all this make you uncomfortable?
- What?

47:39.690 --> 47:40.899
A divorced couples' reunion?

47:43.277 --> 47:44.111
Maybe.

47:48.949 --> 47:50.200
Dinner's ready.

48:35.579 --> 48:37.581
Eat up. I know you like this.

48:51.219 --> 48:54.890
I would never have put something like this
on the table when I lived here.

48:55.557 --> 48:57.351
But now that I'm a guest,
I get to try it here.

48:58.936 --> 49:00.395
Isn't that funny?

49:01.229 --> 49:02.439
Please indulge yourself.

49:02.940 --> 49:04.900
I made it because I heard you liked it.

49:08.403 --> 49:10.113
Do you hate tomatoes too?

49:11.114 --> 49:12.032
That's unexpected.

49:20.666 --> 49:23.877
I thought you would like them.
Aren't people mostly similar?

49:34.012 --> 49:35.347
You've got something here, honey.

49:51.989 --> 49:54.157
How long have you two known Seo-yeon?

49:57.285 --> 49:58.912
About 30 years, I suppose.

49:58.996 --> 50:00.706
That sounds about right.

50:01.289 --> 50:02.332
Wow.

50:03.041 --> 50:05.460
But you were only married two years?

50:06.962 --> 50:09.423
I guess even 30 years together

50:10.173 --> 50:11.341
can't save a marriage.

50:16.346 --> 50:19.725
I guess that's why people say
you're meant for who you're meant for.

50:23.854 --> 50:25.814
- Mr. Yoon Ji-o--
- Have I crossed a line?

50:26.606 --> 50:28.567
I'd rather not play pretend.

50:37.451 --> 50:39.369
How long did you date before marrying?

50:41.371 --> 50:42.205
Well…

50:44.207 --> 50:46.001
that didn't really matter to us.

50:49.838 --> 50:51.590
We hit it off right away.

50:53.633 --> 50:55.052
Wasn't it the same for you guys?

51:23.330 --> 51:24.581
I'm handsome, aren't I?

51:25.874 --> 51:26.708
Young.

51:29.503 --> 51:30.587
And tall too.

51:32.798 --> 51:33.757
What are you doing?

51:35.592 --> 51:37.594
As in, what do I do for a living?

51:37.677 --> 51:39.137
What's my source of income?

51:39.221 --> 51:41.056
Yes, that too.

51:42.766 --> 51:44.101
Uptight curmudgeon.

51:46.520 --> 51:47.854
Do you love Ms. Noh In-ji?

51:52.609 --> 51:54.194
Why the silence?

51:57.030 --> 51:57.989
Just so you know,

51:59.741 --> 52:00.909
I love Lee Seo-yeon.

52:08.416 --> 52:09.751
We've had a lot of wine.

52:13.296 --> 52:14.464
How do you two like it?

52:15.465 --> 52:19.052
We really get into it
after about three glasses.

52:22.013 --> 52:23.473
How about you two?

52:32.691 --> 52:33.733
We prefer beer.

52:38.321 --> 52:40.365
Beer? Really?

52:42.617 --> 52:45.787
I think they have us beat.
Beer has lower alcohol content.

52:53.336 --> 52:56.089
The more I look at it,
the more I prefer the old one. Don't you?

53:03.513 --> 53:04.347
I don't.

53:06.892 --> 53:08.810
That's what I've always found childish
about you.

53:09.561 --> 53:11.021
That's what's wrong with you.

53:11.813 --> 53:14.482
Holding onto the past,
unable to let go of old wounds.

53:16.193 --> 53:17.110
Don't you think?

53:18.361 --> 53:21.573
I knew I should've sold
that fucking pile of crap to a junkyard.

53:27.662 --> 53:29.998
Some things can never be forgotten.

53:30.081 --> 53:31.416
You should watch what you say.

53:37.923 --> 53:38.965
You took it too seriously.

53:39.049 --> 53:41.635
Don't you have any old wounds
you can't let go of?

53:44.721 --> 53:45.639
That's unexpected.

53:57.067 --> 53:58.026
Shall we wrap this up?

53:59.027 --> 54:01.863
I'm not a fan of dragging things out.

54:57.460 --> 55:00.880
Did you see a USB drive in my car?
I couldn't find it.

55:08.388 --> 55:09.597
Don't you use Bluetooth?

55:10.098 --> 55:12.767
I don't like leaving my name
or any kind of trail.

55:16.396 --> 55:17.897
Why don't you use it?

55:20.525 --> 55:22.527
I do, storing my work as I go along.

55:23.111 --> 55:25.530
Security's an issue,
and Bluetooth's a hassle.

55:27.532 --> 55:28.783
I'll plug yours back in.

55:30.368 --> 55:31.870
I listen to it out of habit.

55:34.039 --> 55:35.957
Do you dance to that song?

55:38.418 --> 55:39.252
Tango?

55:43.381 --> 55:45.091
You know it's hard to imagine, right?

55:45.592 --> 55:47.302
You seem like you'd hate
that kind of thing.

55:47.886 --> 55:49.929
You, dancing? I just can't see it.

55:55.852 --> 55:58.730
I apologize. I was being too honest.

56:01.649 --> 56:03.485
Too bad I can't show you.

56:03.568 --> 56:04.861
It would blow your mind.

56:37.018 --> 56:39.145
You did say you'd blow my mind,
didn't you?

57:06.423 --> 57:07.257
What are you…

57:07.757 --> 57:09.426
It takes two to tango.

57:09.509 --> 57:10.885
No, please, no.

57:14.431 --> 57:16.307
The man's right hand
rests on the woman's back,

57:18.059 --> 57:20.937
and his left-hand holds up her right.

57:21.604 --> 57:23.189
Do we really have to…

57:23.273 --> 57:26.443
Let's try moving our center of gravity,
one step at a time.

57:30.905 --> 57:35.618
You never take the steps alone.
You're meant to carry your partner over.

57:35.702 --> 57:38.246
Both our weights
should shift entirely to one side.

57:42.625 --> 57:46.212
Try stepping forward two steps
with your right foot.

57:49.549 --> 57:50.758
- Sorry.
- It's all right.

57:51.885 --> 57:56.639
Right foot forward, another step,
now your left foot.

57:58.141 --> 57:59.684
Step to the side with your right foot.

58:01.352 --> 58:03.730
Change your center of gravity,
then your right foot.

58:09.903 --> 58:10.737
Let's go again.

01:01:37.235 --> 01:01:40.530
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
